---
description: HelpMesh accessibility rules, always apply
alwaysApply: true
---
- This app is for disabled users. Accessibility failures are P0 bugs.
- Use native HTML first. A native `dialog` is fine for a confirm. Do not build dialogs, menus, tabs, or comboboxes from divs.
- Every interactive element: accessible name, keyboard operable, visible 3px focus ring, 48x48px minimum target.
- Never convey information by color alone, sound alone, or hover alone.
- No drag-only, swipe-only, long-press-only, or time-limited interactions.
- Every status change goes through useAnnounce(). On route change, focus the h1 and set document.title.
- Forms: visible labels, aria-describedby for errors, an error summary on submit failure, autocomplete set.
- Text in rem. Layouts reflow to 320px. Respect prefers-reduced-motion, prefers-contrast, and prefers-color-scheme. Never flash content.
- Maps never hold unique information. The list is the primary view.
- Plain language. No blockchain jargon in the primary UI. Say "held safely". Do not show gas, chain, or hex addresses outside Advanced.
- AI output only fills fields the user confirms. Every AI feature has a non-AI path. AI is off in this demo.
- Do not mark a task done if lint, typecheck, or tests fail.
